<article class="env-example" id="0176">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0176">Example <span data-tag="0176">14.11.2</span>.</a> For every $n \geq 0$ we denote $\Delta [n]$ the simplicial set </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \Delta ^{opp} \longrightarrow \textit{Sets},\quad [k] \longmapsto \mathop{\mathrm{Mor}}\nolimits _{\Delta }([k], [n])  \]
</div>
  <p> We leave it to the reader to verify the following statements. Every $m$-simplex of $\Delta [n]$ with $m > n$ is degenerate. There is a unique nondegenerate $n$-simplex of $\Delta [n]$, namely $\text{id}_{[n]}$. </p>
